   "id": "L61mGCakAQAJ",
   "from": "Kerim Çiçek",
   "author": "a0ab5929cb71f914",
   "date": "2022-07-15T21:14:58Z",
   "subject": "should I consider predictor resolution when thinning my records",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "Dear all,<br>I would like to ask a question about the referees’ comments. I thinned my occurrence records 5-km radius buffer around each occurrence record using the spThin. But I used 30 arcsec - 1 km resolution layers as predictors. He/she asks &quot;If the variables are at 1 km, why thinning at 5 km?&quot; should I consider predictor resolution when thinning my records? Is there any thumb of rule about this subject? Any suggestion would be appreciated. Best greets, Kerim<br>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "zHi9qmqoAQAJ",
   "from": "Wallace Ecological Modeling App",
   "author": "881c0dd9c7b0d196",
   "date": "2022-07-15T22:33:10Z",
   "subject": "Re: should I consider predictor resolution when thinning my records",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "Hi Kerim,<div>Yes, you can consider the resolution of predictors when thinning. You can also consider the species biology, such as its dispersal or home range. Spatial thinning aims at reducing errors from sampling bias. More information on thinning can be found here- <a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1111/ecog.01132\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://doi.org/10.1111/ecog.01132&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792489219527000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0hdgh6HtLSKpG_704XNHY7\">https://doi.org/10.1111/ecog.01132</a>, the Aiello-Lammens et al. paper on the spThin R-package and spatial thinning for ecological niche modeling.</div><div>-Bethany<br><br></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"auto\" class=\"gmail_attr\">On Friday, July 15, 2022 at 5:14:58 PM UTC-4 <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">krm...@gmail.com</a> wrote:<br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\">Dear all,<br>I would like to ask a question about the referees’ comments. I thinned my occurrence records 5-km radius buffer around each occurrence record using the spThin. But I used 30 arcsec - 1 km resolution layers as predictors. He/she asks &quot;If the variables are at 1 km, why thinning at 5 km?&quot; should I consider predictor resolution when thinning my records? Is there any thumb of rule about this subject? Any suggestion would be appreciated. Best greets, Kerim<br></blockquote></div>"
    ]
